public static int calculateEnergy(String s) {
    int maxLength = 0;
    int currentLength = 0;
    char previousChar = '\0';
    for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
        if (c == previousChar) {
            currentLength++;
        } else {
            maxLength = Math.max(maxLength, currentLength);
            currentLength = 1;
        }
        previousChar = c;
    }
    return maxLength;
}
```
This code uses a single loop to iterate through the characters of the input string. It maintains two variables: `maxLength` to store the maximum length of a substring containing only one character, and `currentLength` to store the length of the current substring.

The loop checks if the current character is the same as the previous character. If it is, it increments the `currentLength` variable. If it's not, it updates the `maxLength` variable with the maximum of the current `maxLength` and `currentLength`, and resets the `currentLength` variable to 1.

At the end of the loop, the `maxLength` variable will contain the maximum length of a substring containing only one character, which is the energy of the input string.

